            <ArticleTitle>Direct explanations for the development and use of a multi-layer perceptron network that classifies low-back-pain patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>335-47</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Using a new method published by the first author, this article shows how direct explanations can be provided to interpret the classification of any input case by a standard multilayer perceptron (MLP) network. The method is demonstrated for a real-world MLP that classifies low-back-pain patients into three diagnostic classes. The application of the method leads to the discovery of a number of mis-diagnosed training and test cases and to the development of a more optimal low-back-pain MLP network.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
